{"book":{"id":"book-slavery-in-indian-country-the-changing-face-of-captivity-in-early-america-christina-snyder","slug":"slavery-in-indian-country-the-changing-face-of-captivity-in-early-america-christina-snyder","title":"Slavery in Indian Country: The Changing Face of Captivity in Early America","authors":[{"id":"person-christina-snyder","name":"Christina Snyder"}],"publisherId":"publisher-harvard-university-press","imprintId":"imprint-harvard-university-press","isbn13":["9780674064232"],"subjects":["History"],"topics":["Indigenous History","Slavery & Emancipation","Gender & Feminism","Money, Markets & Economic Policy"],"centralFigures":[],"links":{"amazon":"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Slavery%20in%20Indian%20Country%3A%20The%20Changing%20Face%20of%20Captivity%20in%20Early%20America%20Christina%20Snyder","bookshop":"https://bookshop.org/search?keywords=Slavery%20in%20Indian%20Country%3A%20The%20Changing%20Face%20of%20Captivity%20in%20Early%20America%20Christina%20Snyder","indiebound":"https://www.indiebound.org/search/book?keys=Slavery%20in%20Indian%20Country%3A%20The%20Changing%20Face%20of%20Captivity%20in%20Early%20America%20Christina%20Snyder","worldcat":"https://search.worldcat.org/search?q=Slavery%20in%20Indian%20Country%3A%20The%20Changing%20Face%20of%20Captivity%20in%20Early%20America%20Christina%20Snyder","publisher":"https://books.google.com/books/about/Slavery_in_Indian_Country.html?hl=&id=DyQvEAAAQBAJ"},"sourceIds":["source-award-record-frederick-douglass-slavery-abolition-gilder-lehrman-center-official-past-winners-and-finalists-a","source-award-record-oah-frederick-jackson-turner-award-oah-frederick-jackson-turner-award-official-page-internet-arc","source-google-books-slavery-in-indian-country-the-changing-face-of-captivity-in-early-america-christina-snyder","source-open-library-slavery-in-indian-country-the-changing-face-of-captivity-in-early-america-christina-snyder","source-cover-open-library-slavery-in-indian-country-the-changing-face-of-captivity-in-early-america-christina-snyder","source-imprint-normalization"],"subjectCategories":[{"source":"google_books","scheme":"google_books_category","label":"History","sourceId":"source-google-books-slavery-in-indian-country-the-changing-face-of-captivity-in-early-america-christina-snyder"}],"publicationYear":2012,"pageCount":342,"summary":"Slavery existed in North America long before the first Africans arrived at Jamestown in 1619. For centuries, from the pre-Columbian era through the 1840s, Native Americans took prisoners of war and killed, adopted, or enslaved them. Christina Snyder's pathbreaking book takes a familiar setting for bondage, the American South, and places Native Americans at the center of her engrossing story. Indian warriors captured a wide range of enemies, including Africans, Europeans, and other Indians. Yet until the late eighteenth century, age and gender more than race affected the fate of captives. As economic and political crises mounted, however, Indians began to racialize slavery and target African Americans. Native people struggling to secure a separate space for themselves in America developed a shared language of race with white settlers.","thumbnailUrl":"/book-covers/book-slavery-in-indian-country-the-changing-face-of-captivity-in-early-america-christina-snyder.jpg","displaySummary":"For centuries, from the pre-Columbian era through the 1840s, Native Americans took prisoners of war and killed, adopted, or enslaved them. Christina Snyder's pathbreaking book takes a familiar setting for bondage, the American South, and places Native Americans at the center of her engrossing story. Indian warriors captured a wide range of enemies, including Africans, Europeans, and other Indians. Yet until the late eighteenth century, age and gender more than race affected the fate of captives. As economic and political crises mounted, however, Indians began to racialize slavery and target African Americans. Native people struggling to secure a separate spac